   "id": "approach",
   "title": "The Allies march in from the east",
   "time": "02:00 to 06:00",
   "narrative": "Forty squadrons of Allied cavalry leave camp at 02:00, and at 03:00 the main army follows in eight columns across the Kessel. By about 06:00 the head of the march reaches Schwenningen, three kilometres from Blindheim, where troops who held the village overnight form a ninth column. Marlborough and Eugene agree the plan: Marlborough, with 36,000 men, will take on Tallard, while Eugene's 16,000 will hold Marsin and the Elector. Tallard, fooled by prisoners' tales, believes the Allies are about to withdraw.",
