   "title": "Both armies take position",
   "time": "08:00 to 11:00",
   "narrative": "Signal guns recall the French foragers and the army forms behind the Nebel. Maffei holds Lutzingen with five Bavarian battalions and sixteen guns, Rozel's seven French battalions stand in the woods beside it, and cavalry fill the gap to Oberglauheim, packed with fourteen battalions under Blainville. Tallard draws his horse up between that village and Blindheim, where Clérambault holds nine battalions. The Allies form beyond the stream, taking cannon fire for hours; many of their generals doubt the attack can succeed.",
