  {
   "id": "cutts1",
   "title": "Cutts's first assault on Blindheim",
   "time": "13:00",
   "narrative": "By 10:00 Cutts has cleared two mills on the stream and sits in front of Blindheim under a six-gun battery. At 13:00 Rowe's brigade advances silently across about 150 metres. The French hold their fire until thirty metres and then deliver a deadly volley; Rowe falls mortally wounded. Small parties break in but are thrown out, and the Gens d'Armes ride down on the exposed flank until Wilkes's Hessians stand firm and drive them off.",
