  {
   "id": "cutts2",
   "title": "The village is crammed with men",
   "time": "Early afternoon",
   "narrative": "The Allies rally and storm again, and again fail. The repeated blows panic Clérambault, who without asking Tallard orders his reserve battalions into Blindheim. The village fills so tightly that, in one French officer's words, the men could not even fire, and the garrison loses the power to move. Marlborough sees the mistake and cancels a third assault: Cutts is merely to contain the village, and no more than 5,000 Allies hold twice that number of French in place.",
